in Japan town  in San Francisco to the vitaliy a very  high-end Hotel in the financial district  over the course of the quarter century  we created 52 boutique hotels yeah they  went swimming oh yeah I think CEOs are  chief emotions officers because I think  more than anything what we need to  understand as leaders is how do we  motivate our people and how do we  satisfy our guests and behind both of  those is understanding their needs so  the way you create meaning for someone  who's made in a hotel or cooking a  kitchen you help them to see that the  work that they're doing is having an  impact on the customer so what that  means is you need to have customers come  in and talk to your staff very few  companies do this what we've done over  the course of a long period of time is  just make sure that we're broadcasting  stories from guests sometimes it's in an  email  sometimes it's face to face at a staff  meeting so that our employees can  actually hear the impact of their work  the best thing you can do is to label  your emotions label your emotions  understand where you are because it  takes you to a different place in your  brain what I learned along the way is  that understanding people and  understanding myself is probably the  most important gift I learned from  Business School and then it's probably  the most important thing I learned along  the way thank you very much
 

